# Trivy vulnerability exceptions for the Docker image built from api/Dockerfile.
# Add a CVE ID per line with a comment explaining why it's accepted, e.g.:
# CVE-2023-12345  # false positive, not reachable in our usage — see <link>

# multer 2.2.0, nested inside @nestjs/platform-express (not our own direct
# multer@2.4.0, which is already patched — see api/package.json). The real
# fix needs NestJS v12, but @nestjs/throttler (used app-wide for rate
# limiting: login, contact form, booking) only declares peer support up to
# @nestjs/core ^11 as of its latest release (6.5.0) — no v12-compatible
# release exists yet. Forcing the mismatch would ship the rate-limiter
# against a range its own maintainers haven't validated. Exposure is
# limited: the only multer-backed endpoint (gallery photo upload) sits
# behind AdminAuthGuard, not public. Revisit once @nestjs/throttler ships
# v12 support — check `npm view @nestjs/throttler versions`.
CVE-2026-77037
CVE-2026-77078
CVE-2026-82333
